# Component & Styling Patterns

## Shared Style Factories (`src/common/index.ts`)
Always compose Windows 95 UI surfaces using shared helpers from `../common` and sizes from `../common/system`:
- `createBoxStyles({ background, color })` — Standard box sizing, `theme.material` background, and `theme.materialText` color.
- `createBorderStyles({ style, invert })` — 3D bevel borders (`'button' | 'buttonPressed' | 'buttonThin' | 'buttonThinPressed' | 'field' | 'grouping' | 'status' | 'window'`) with `box-shadow` support via `$shadow` / `shadow`.
- `createFlatBoxStyles()` — Flat variant styling (`theme.canvas`, `theme.flatLight`, `theme.flatDark`).
- `createDisabledTextStyles()` — Disabled text fill and `1px 1px` shadow (`theme.materialTextDisabled`, `theme.materialTextDisabledShadow`).
- `createHatchedBackground({ mainColor, secondaryColor, pixelSize })` — Checkerboard/dithered pattern.
- `createScrollbars(variant)` — Custom Windows 95 webkit scrollbars (`'default' | 'flat'`).
- `focusOutline()` — `2px dotted ${theme.materialText}` focus indicator.
- `blockSizes` (`src/common/system.ts`) — Standard control heights (`sm: '28px'`, `md: '36px'`, `lg: '44px'`).

## Transient Props & `shouldForwardProp`
Prevent custom props from reaching the DOM using transient `$` props or `withConfig`:

```tsx
// ✅ Pattern A: Transient ($) props for internal styled elements
const StyledFrame = styled.div<
  { $variant: NonNullable<FrameProps['variant']> } & CommonThemeProps
>`
  ${({ $variant }) => createFrameStyles($variant)}
`;

// ✅ Pattern B: shouldForwardProp Set for exported styled components
const buttonFilteredProps = new Set([
  'active',
  'fullWidth',
  'primary',
  'size',
  'square',
  'variant'
]);

export const StyledButton = styled.button.withConfig({
  shouldForwardProp: prop => !buttonFilteredProps.has(prop)
})<StyledButtonProps>`...`;
```

## Shared Hooks, Utilities & Prop Conventions
- Extend `CommonStyledProps` (`as` prop support) and native HTML element attributes (using `Omit<React.HTMLAttributes<...>, ...>` when overriding event signatures).
- Reuse `StyledInput`, `StyledLabel`, and `LabelText` from `src/common/SwitchBase.ts` for toggle/checkable controls (`Checkbox`, `Radio`, `TreeView`).
- Guard interactive handlers when `disabled` is true (e.g., `onClick={disabled ? undefined : onClick}` and default `onTouchStart = noOp`).
- Use shared utilities in `src/common/utils/`: `noOp`, `clamp`, `getSize`, `roundValueToStep`, `mapFromWindowsTheme`, and event type guards (`isReactFocusEvent`, `isReactKeyboardEvent`, `isReactMouseEvent`).
- Use shared hooks in `src/common/hooks/`:
  - `useControlledOrUncontrolled` for components supporting both `value` + `onChange` and `defaultValue`.
  - `useId` for accessible deterministic/SSR-safe IDs.
  - `useForkRef` to merge internal refs with forwarded refs.
  - `useEventCallback` and `useIsFocusVisible` for stable event handlers and keyboard focus rings.
